
# Grid — headless responsive grid, ported from the React grid family (mesh/deck/face/code/component/grid). The
# container is a CSS grid; the column count comes from the pure `compute-fit` logic (logic/grid) fed by the measured
# container width, applied as a reactive `columns` style/class. Parts: grid (container), grid-item. The theme owns
# display:grid + gap; `columns` drives grid-template-columns. The JS-measured + virtualized variants (block / flow /
# virtual) add a ResizeObserver + scroll windowing on top (a dom primitive, the remaining piece); the CSS-grid base
# here is fully headless + ready to theme.

load @cluesurf/site/code/zone/render
  find element
load @cluesurf/site/code/dom/dom
  find view
  find append

zone grid
  take host, like view
  take class
  take columns
  zone div
    bind data-slot, text <grid>
    bind data-columns, read columns
    bind class, read class
    slot

zone grid-item
  take host, like view
  take class
  zone div
    bind data-slot, text <grid-item>
    bind class, read class
    slot
